    },
    "body": "While stress-testing #36147 I noticed sporadic port collisions still occurring on FreeBSD.\n\n`set_ephemeral_port_range()` keeps the source port out of the test port range, but only for sockets the framework creates itself. Python's `http.client` creates its sockets internally, so RPC and REST connections can still be given a source port inside the test range. A connection to a closed port can then connect to itself. For example, the wrong-RPC-port startup check failed with `BadStatusLine: POST / HTTP/1.1` because the client read back its own request.\n\nThis change adds a `netutil.HTTPConnection` subclass that sets the port range before connecting, and uses it in `AuthServiceProxy` and in the tests that open HTTP connections directly.\n\nHTTPS is left unchanged because we don't serve RPC over TLS so it seems unnecessary.",
